	)
  (text "HPOUTN intentionally left no-connect (corrected back, 2026-09-29 -\nthis sheet briefly used both HPOUTP/HPOUTN differentially into the\nBOOM MIC / TX SELECT sheet's transformer, then reverted to\nsingle-ended HPOUTP only). A series blocking cap on that sheet now\nhandles what the differential connection used to handle for free:\nHPOUTP sits at the DAC's ~0.85V common-mode bias, and driving a\ntransformer primary single-ended (other leg tied to AGND, not\nHPOUTN) would push that DC across the winding as a continuous\n~7mA bias current toward core saturation. The cap blocks it.\nResidual, not resolved by the cap: the ADAU186x Hardware Reference\nManual (UG-2257) documents this output stage as DIFFERENTIAL ONLY -\ninputs get an explicit single-ended mode and register bit\n(AINx_INPUT_MODE), the DAC/headphone/line output never does, in\nprose or in the HP_CTRL register map. Running single-ended is\ntherefore an undocumented configuration, not a specified one - the\ncap fixes the DC problem, it doesn't make this a supported mode.\nJ1 pin 4 (previously spare) carries GPIO_RLY_TX_SEL_3V3 to that\nsheet's relay driver.\n\nThat sheet was renamed AIRCRAFT AUDIO I/O 2026-09-30 (still page 2,\nsame file) when an earphone/RX audio mute relay was added alongside\nthe original boom-mic/TX circuit. J1 pin 8 (the other pin left spare\nby the SPT1/3V3_CM5 cleanup above) now carries GPIO_RLY_RX_MUTE_3V3\nto that relay's driver - a deliberately independent GPIO from pin 4,\nper Peter, so the two relays can be sequenced separately in\nfirmware. Neither pin is spare on J1 any longer."
    (at 288.29 180 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid "1ef2d43a-8c92-489d-8456-ec13372ee2a2")
  )
